WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
India, about the second century.

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:07.760
A monk named Nagarjuna writes
27 chapters of short verses.

3
00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:11.830
His target: the idea that
anything has a nature of its own,

4
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.870
that exists by itself.

5
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.400
His claim: nothing does.

6
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.670
Critics called this nihilism.

7
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.400
If all is empty, they
asked, does anything matter?

8
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:27.210
So if nothing has a nature of its
own, how can anything be true at all?

9
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.100
In this mission, you'll
follow Nagarjuna's argument,

10
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.600
step by step.

11
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:36.380
Then you'll weigh his boldest claim: there
is not the slightest difference between

12
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.690
samsara and nirvana.

13
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.470
Your mission: find out how anything can
be true if nothing has a nature of its

14
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:43.960
own.
